From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: Don't WARN when a GEM mapping cannot get its
 pages

panfrost_mmu_map() is called when a BO is opened or first used by a job.
drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt() fails with -ENOMEM when shmem cannot
allocate the backing pages, for instance when the caller's memory cgroup
is at its limit. That is an ordinary allocation failure that userspace
already handles (Mesa reports "DRM_IOCTL_PANFROST_CREATE_BO failed
(err=12)"), not a driver bug, but the WARN_ON() turns it into a kernel
warning with a backtrace:

  WARNING: drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c:478 at panfrost_mmu_map+0xcc

It is easy to hit with dEQP-GLES31 draw_indirect compute_interop large
cases on a 1 GB board. Return the error without warning; no pages are
held at this point, so there is nothing to undo.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
index 4a3162c..575a4d5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ int panfrost_mmu_map(struct panfrost_gem_mapping *mapping)
 		prot |= IOMMU_NOEXEC;
 
 	sgt = drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt(shmem);
-	if (WARN_ON(IS_ERR(sgt)))
+	if (IS_ERR(sgt))
 		return PTR_ERR(sgt);
 
 	ret = mmu_map_sg(pfdev, mapping->mmu, mapping->mmnode.start << PAGE_SHIFT,
-- 
2.43.0

